### Request ID and response transformation (unit 5.7)
### Passwords come from .env.

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo-user",
  "password": "<DEMO_USER_PASSWORD from .env>"
}

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. No ID sent: the response carries a generated UUID in X-Request-Id,
### plus X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and no Server header.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3. A well-formed ID is kept: the response header is client-trace-42.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Request-Id: client-trace-42

### 4. A malformed ID (spaces, markup) is replaced by a generated UUID.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-Request-Id: bad id <script>

### 5. A gateway-generated error also carries the ID: 401 without a token.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
